@ 17.10.1.3 - Proto-Indo-Aryan to Northwestern Middle Indo-Aryan
# citation: Pogostick Man, from Shukla, Shaligram (1974), “Phonological change and dialect variation in Middle-Indo-Aryan”. In Anderson, J., and C. Jones (Eds.), Historical Linguistics II:391-401.
	C(C) > ∅ / C_#
	{ VN, VC:[-nas] } > { V:[+nas], V:[+long] } / _#
	{ a{i,j}(a), a{u,w}(a) } > { e, o }
	{ j, w } > { d͡ʒ, b } / V_V
	C > C:[+voice] / V_V
	{bʱ,dʱ,ɡʱ} > h / V_V
	{j,v} > ∅ / V_V
	Vm > Vv / _V
	Vv > V:[+nas]v / _V
	{ e, o } > { i, u } / _#
	V:[+long] > V:[-long] / _#
	ah > o
	ɽ > i
	kʂ > t͡ʃ:[+long]
	{ʂ,ç} > s
	sC > Ch
	v > ∅ / :{ t_, d_ }:
	CC > CC / V_V
	Cn > CC / V_V // C = d͡ʒ
	d͡ʒɲ > ɳ:[+long] / V_V